// Per-construct DSL layout: every <kind>s.memql file in a domain
// holds every construct of that kind in the domain. This domain's
// concepts live in concepts.memql; this file carries its reads.

// ---- codeMetricsInWindow (memql#4208) ----
//
// The client read over the continuous-aggregate rollups: one bucket, one
// [windowStart, windowEnd) range, selected by codeReference PREFIX (a
// module's fqnPrefixes -- "starts with ANY of") or by one exact
// codeReference. Before this existed the portal's per-module drill-in
// walked the generic concept browse newest-first under a 3 x 200 cap and
// joined client-side; on a busy cluster a module's history scrolled out
// of the cap. This is the server-side read that cap stood in for.
//
// Selection, never a pass-through. `codeReference startsWith
// args.prefixes` matches nothing for an empty list and for a list of
// blanks (the engine rule, component/memql/executor_filter.go), and the
// exact key is a when()-guarded equality, so a call with no prefixes and
// no codeReference returns an EMPTY result rather than a cluster-wide
// scan. prefixes is REQUIRED precisely so that an absent list is a refused
// call and never an unconstrained one; an empty list is accepted.
//
// Authz: codeMetric declares no @rowAuthz tier and carries no user-scope
// field. This read carries the same gate the generic concept browse gives
// the concept today -- any authenticated caller -- by design (memql#4208:
// "same read gate as codeMetric today"). It lands in the conformance
// "other" bucket beside the cluster-topology reads and is listed on the
// undeclared-tier ratchet under its own issue.
//
// Order: rows come back in row.createdAt order under a keyset cursor (a
// payload sort key is not keyset-eligible), which is what lets a client
// walk the whole window to exhaustion with no cap; the caller orders by
// windowStart. The caller aligns windowStart / windowEnd to the bucket.

/// codeMetric rows for one bucket inside [windowStart, windowEnd), selected by codeReference
/// prefix (ANY of prefixes) or by the exact codeReference. An empty prefixes list with no
/// codeReference returns nothing. Keyset-paged in row.createdAt order; order by windowStart
/// client-side.
query codeMetric codeMetricsInWindow {
  args {
    /// codeReference prefixes to match (a module's fqnPrefixes). Required so an absent list is
    /// refused; an empty list matches nothing.
    prefixes       []string!
    /// Optional exact codeReference, matched in addition to the prefixes.
    codeReference  string
    /// Which continuous aggregate the rows came from.
    bucket         enum("1m", "1h")!
    /// Inclusive window start, aligned to the bucket by the caller.
    windowStart    datetime!
    /// Exclusive window end, aligned to the bucket by the caller.
    windowEnd      datetime!
  }
  filter  bucket==args.bucket && windowStart>=args.windowStart && windowStart<args.windowEnd && (when(args.codeReference) { codeReference==args.codeReference } || codeReference startsWith args.prefixes)
  sort     "row.createdAt", "asc"
  paginate 500
}
